                <pb facs="1000" n="992" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg992"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.417/1103: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-06T14:00:00+09:00">December 6, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 6—9:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1281. Department’s 457, November 8, 4 p.m. In a formal note dated December 2 the
                    Foreign Office informs us that the Japanese Government has given notice of
                    abrogation of the Fur Seal Convention of 1911 to all the signatories.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
